  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved the institutional policy or regulatory framework strengthen governance, financial management or sustainability for the delivery of gender equitable social protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO has been providing technical assistance to the National Insurance Board of Trinidad and Tobago (NIBTT) for actuarial valuations of social security schemes. This includes the 11th Actuarial Valuation of the National Insurance Fund, preparation of a Funding Policy paper, and a Cost Assessment for an Unemployment Insurance scheme, all completed by September 2022. As of June 2024, the ILO performed a 12th Actuarial Review for the NIBTT due to finish in early 2026. This will help ensure long-term financial sustainability, considering the adequacy of benefits provided by the NIBTT under Convention 102 on Social Security (Minimum Standards). Gender equality principles will be integrated into the social security domain.                                                                         
                                                                                                                                                                                 The ILO&apos;s support includes technical assistance, expert advice, advocacy, training, and facilitation, with coordination from SOCPRO and potential involvement of ITC/ILO for training activities. External consultants will assist in interventions, guided by ILO Conventions, Resolutions, and Codes of Practice, along with regional and global best practices. This collaboration aims to benefit the NIBTT and enhance the social protection framework in Trinidad and Tobago. The ministry of Labour is working towards the ratification of the Social Security (Minimum Standards) Convention, 1952 (No. 102), with technical support from the ILO.</narrative>
  </description>
